{
  "format": 1,
  "about": "Which http connector entries reach a run, and what a person approves for each (M69.1). An entry merges as type, url, headers (sorted), oauth (sorted) and timeout, and nothing else it holds. oauth passes only clientId (1-256 printable ASCII), callbackPort (a whole number 1-65535), authServerMetadataUrl (https://, a host of letters, digits, . and - with an optional :port, then printable ASCII but space, at most 2048) and scopes (one string, 1-1024 printable ASCII); any other key, or an oauth that is not an object, is malformed, and an empty one is none. timeout is absent or a whole number of milliseconds from 1000 to 600000. A malformed entry has no key and is never merged, since one invalid field makes Claude Code refuse the whole --mcp-config. The key is the sha256 hex of JSON [name, \"http\", url, headerPairs], with a fifth element of oauth pairs sorted by key when oauth is present; timeout is never in it. Replayed by replays_the_shared_connector_approvals in src-tauri/src/connectors.rs and by src/engine/connectors.test.ts. The Linear and Notion cases are the presets as shipped; every other name and URL is synthetic. `why` is for the reader.",
